# Asterix & Obelix: Slap Them All! (PPSA08576): cross the logos, the title screen and the menus into
# the first forest level. Seconds are measured from the first pad poll. These are exactly the Cross
# anchors recorded in issue #1601; no directional input is needed.
#
# Observed on a Linux hardware-Vulkan boot through tools/snapshot at PROSPER_RENDER_SCALE=4
# (480x270), sampling once per second: black to 6s, publisher/engine logos 7-17s, black 18s, an
# intro screen 20-23s, the title screen and menus 25-39s, a black load 40-44s, then the first forest
# level from 45.1s, fading in over 45-48s (40,234 colours at 45.1s, then about 70,900) and settling
# from 49.1s. Gameplay then holds unbroken to the end of the profiled 209s capture: all 161 samples
# from 49.1s onward measure 74,569-75,235 distinct colours at 0.9975-0.9991 coverage, with no black
# frame, no fade and no transition anywhere in that span.
#
# Asterix idles rather than walking under this route, so the level is rendered with both character
# portraits, health and rage gauges, score and TOP score, the parallax forest and the blinking GO!
# prompt. That is the milestone this route exists to protect ("title and first forest level"), and
# consecutive samples still differ because of the idle animation, the wandering rabbit and the
# blinking prompt: the 60-frame guard window measured 59 pixel changes -- the maximum possible -- in
# both verify runs and in the checks that reported it.
#
# The snapshot guard asterix-gameplay samples 70-130s, well inside that span.
3:cross
